# Vanilla Minecraft Pickaxe Head - Accurate mesh model
# Based on pickaxe.json weapon profile
# All coordinates in centimeters
# Pickaxe oriented PERPENDICULAR to handle
#
# Dimensions from JSON:
# Eye: 60mm (6cm) length, 40mm (4cm) height, 20mm (2cm) thickness
# Front spike: 160mm (16cm) length, 40mm (4cm) base width/height
# Rear spike: 160mm (16cm) length, 40mm (4cm) base width/height
#
# Coordinate system for perpendicular head:
# - X-axis: along the spike direction (primary axis)
# - Y-axis: handle direction (vertical when attached)
# - Z-axis: secondary horizontal
# - Origin: center of eye where handle passes through

# ==============================================================
# EYE SECTION (central hub where handle passes through)
# Eye: 6cm long (X), 4cm tall (Y), 2cm thick (Z)
# ==============================================================

# Eye vertices - rectangular prism
# Back of eye (-X side)
v -3.0 -2.0 1.0
v -3.0 -2.0 -1.0
v -3.0 2.0 1.0
v -3.0 2.0 -1.0

# Front of eye (+X side)
v 3.0 -2.0 1.0
v 3.0 -2.0 -1.0
v 3.0 2.0 1.0
v 3.0 2.0 -1.0

# ==============================================================
# FRONT SPIKE (extends in +X direction from eye)
# 16cm length, tapers from 4cm x 4cm base to point
# ==============================================================

# Spike at 1/4 length (4cm from eye)
v 7.0 -1.5 0.75
v 7.0 -1.5 -0.75
v 7.0 1.5 0.75
v 7.0 1.5 -0.75

# Spike at 1/2 length (8cm from eye)
v 11.0 -1.0 0.5
v 11.0 -1.0 -0.5
v 11.0 1.0 0.5
v 11.0 1.0 -0.5

# Spike at 3/4 length (12cm from eye)
v 15.0 -0.5 0.25
v 15.0 -0.5 -0.25
v 15.0 0.5 0.25
v 15.0 0.5 -0.25

# Front spike tip (19cm from origin = 3cm eye + 16cm spike)
v 19.0 0.0 0.0

# ==============================================================
# REAR SPIKE (extends in -X direction from eye)
# Same dimensions as front spike
# ==============================================================

# Spike at 1/4 length (4cm from eye, in -X)
v -7.0 -1.5 0.75
v -7.0 -1.5 -0.75
v -7.0 1.5 0.75
v -7.0 1.5 -0.75

# Spike at 1/2 length (8cm from eye)
v -11.0 -1.0 0.5
v -11.0 -1.0 -0.5
v -11.0 1.0 0.5
v -11.0 1.0 -0.5

# Spike at 3/4 length (12cm from eye)
v -15.0 -0.5 0.25
v -15.0 -0.5 -0.25
v -15.0 0.5 0.25
v -15.0 0.5 -0.25

# Rear spike tip (19cm from origin in -X)
v -19.0 0.0 0.0

# ==============================================================
# FACES (triangles, CCW winding for outward normals)
# ==============================================================

# ---- EYE TOP AND BOTTOM ----
# Top face
f 3 7 8
f 3 8 4
# Bottom face
f 1 2 6
f 1 6 5
# Front side (+Z)
f 1 5 7
f 1 7 3
# Back side (-Z)
f 2 4 8
f 2 8 6

# ---- EYE to FRONT SPIKE 1/4 ----
# Top
f 7 11 12
f 7 12 8
# Bottom
f 5 6 10
f 5 10 9
# Front (+Z)
f 5 9 11
f 5 11 7
# Back (-Z)
f 6 8 12
f 6 12 10

# ---- FRONT SPIKE 1/4 to 1/2 ----
# Top
f 11 15 16
f 11 16 12
# Bottom
f 9 10 14
f 9 14 13
# Front (+Z)
f 9 13 15
f 9 15 11
# Back (-Z)
f 10 12 16
f 10 16 14

# ---- FRONT SPIKE 1/2 to 3/4 ----
# Top
f 15 19 20
f 15 20 16
# Bottom
f 13 14 18
f 13 18 17
# Front (+Z)
f 13 17 19
f 13 19 15
# Back (-Z)
f 14 16 20
f 14 20 18

# ---- FRONT SPIKE 3/4 to TIP ----
# Four triangular faces converging to point
f 17 21 19
f 18 20 21
f 17 18 21
f 19 21 20

# ---- EYE to REAR SPIKE 1/4 ----
# Top
f 3 4 25
f 3 25 24
# Bottom
f 1 23 2
f 1 22 23
# Front (+Z)
f 1 3 24
f 1 24 22
# Back (-Z)
f 2 23 25
f 2 25 4

# ---- REAR SPIKE 1/4 to 1/2 ----
# Top
f 24 25 29
f 24 29 28
# Bottom
f 22 27 23
f 22 26 27
# Front (+Z)
f 22 24 28
f 22 28 26
# Back (-Z)
f 23 27 29
f 23 29 25

# ---- REAR SPIKE 1/2 to 3/4 ----
# Top
f 28 29 33
f 28 33 32
# Bottom
f 26 31 27
f 26 30 31
# Front (+Z)
f 26 28 32
f 26 32 30
# Back (-Z)
f 27 31 33
f 27 33 29

# ---- REAR SPIKE 3/4 to TIP ----
# Four triangular faces converging to point
f 30 32 34
f 31 34 33
f 30 34 31
f 32 33 34
